      "writtenOn": "2024-11-21T15:06:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we want to enforce that sampledTextureBinding is only set for the Vulkan backend here? My understanding is this is specific to Vulkan COMBINED_IMAGE_SAMPLERs and implementation doesn\u0027t exist in other backends. I\u0027m also not sure if frontend validation should enforce a specific backend for features?",
      "revId": "729d16fa67944981ad5bf7aeaffe73efd2982156",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "281970b7_93ec504c",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/BindGroupLayoutInternal.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 213,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-22T14:57:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general the frontend should be the one to gate on a specific Feature being present. That said, this feature should happen to work on other backends where StaticSamplers is supported because everything `sampledTextureBinding` does is constrain on the validation side that the sampler be statically used only with that texture, so we can do the correct thing in Vulkan. Because it is just opting in to additional constraints, it will work everywhere.",
      "parentUuid": "c0eecaf6_488ebc73",
      "revId": "729d16fa67944981ad5bf7aeaffe73efd2982156",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
