      "writtenOn": "2024-11-26T13:30:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like I\u0027m missing something. From what I understand, `sampledTextureBinding` doesn\u0027t need to be implemented in other backends because it will just happen to work. There are two parts to `sampledTextureBinding` for Vulkan YCbCr: the frontend validation that checks that the static sampler / texture are only used together (or not at all), and the Vulkan backend part which uses that information to make the combined-texture-sampler when creating the BindGroup.\n\nOtherwise in terms of WGSL, or BindGroup bindings, the sampler is \"just\" a static sampler, and the texture view is just a texture view. So if they are used together, things will just happen to work in other backends. What the developer tells us with `sampledTextureBinding` is a (validated) promise that it will use them only together, and we use that promise for YCbCr in Vulkan.",
      "parentUuid": "49ee0fcc_0f85eb8d",
      "revId": "729d16fa67944981ad5bf7aeaffe73efd2982156",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
